From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TurboVadim <yolkin.vadim@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 11:35:04 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Mirror hot synced entity data in plain fields

Entity flags, air, freeze ticks, no-gravity and pose, mob flags (NoAI,
left-handed, aggressive), the sleeping position and the dropped item
stack were read from SynchedEntityData every tick: holder, item array,
data item and boxed value, four dependent loads each. Entities now keep
plain copies, filled right after the synced data is built and updated by
SynchedEntityData on every value write through a SyncedDataHolder hook
that passes the item's own accessor, so look-alike accessors with the
same id stay covered. The health mirror moves onto the same hook and
drops its initialisation flag.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/network/syncher/SyncedDataHolder.java b/net/minecraft/network/syncher/SyncedDataHolder.java
index 93c2e47e4860a27156ddf1434bd9c1e5a6eba744..7467ad66cc182cce3aaa6dec1ae963a1b338231f 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/network/syncher/SyncedDataHolder.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/network/syncher/SyncedDataHolder.java
@@ -6,4 +6,8 @@ public interface SyncedDataHolder {
     void onSyncedDataUpdated(EntityDataAccessor<?> accessor);
 
     void onSyncedDataUpdated(List<SynchedEntityData.DataValue<?>> updatedItems);
+
+    // Pyzh - Mirror hot synced entity data; called after every value write with the item's own accessor
+    default void pyzh$onSyncedValueWritten(final EntityDataAccessor<?> accessor, final Object value) {
+    }
 }
diff --git a/net/minecraft/network/syncher/SynchedEntityData.java b/net/minecraft/network/syncher/SynchedEntityData.java
